      "week": 6,
      "day": 37,
      "title": "Ponferrada -> Villafranca del Bierzo",
  "distance": "24,6 km",
  "time": "5 hours 48 min",
  "short_desc": "Gentle shortcut and a taste of luxury",
  "long_desc": " After a delicious breakfast, we spent the morning strolling through the streets of Ponferrada, soaking in the charm of the city. Over dinner the night before and again at breakfast, we had the pleasure of chatting with Nancy and Dave, a lovely couple from Fort Lauderdale, Florida, who are walking the Camino for 10 days before heading home via a 14 days cruise. To save Roy’s back and give our legs a break, we opted for a short taxi ride to the nearby village of Cacabelos, just outside Ponferrada. From there, we continued on foot through beautiful vineyards under a clear sky. By afternoon, the temperature hit 25°C and we were both hot, tired, and more than ready for food and rest. We arrived at our destination, Villafranca del Bierzo, where we checked into the Parador Hotel a very welcome touch of comfort on the Camino. The hotel has both an indoor and outdoor pool, although only the indoor one was open. We were reminded of a lovely conversation we had back in Atapuerca with an American diplomat’s wife from Kingston, Jamaica, who had also sung the praises of the Parador hotels. It seems we share a taste for their peaceful charm. The day ended with a delicious dinner at the hotel, a perfect way to wrap up another memorable step on our journey.",
      "accommodation": "Parador Villafranca de Bierzo",
